<details class="publication-mobile-toc"><summary>On this page</summary><a href="#verdict">Verdict</a><a href="#product">What Freshdesk is</a><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a><a href="#strengths">Strengths</a><a href="#tradeoffs">Trade-offs</a><a href="#fit">Best fit</a><a href="#setup">Setup and migration</a><a href="#method">Methodology</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></details>
<p>Freshdesk is an email-first help desk from Freshworks. It brings support requests into a ticketing workflow and includes shared inbox, customer portal, knowledge base and reporting features in its published plans. Its appeal is the familiar ticket model and clear per-agent plan ladder. The main checks are whether the email-first product covers your channels, whether your plan includes the controls you need, and how AI usage affects the final bill.</p>
<h2 id="verdict">Verdict: who should shortlist Freshdesk?</h2><p>Freshdesk is worth evaluating for small and mid-sized teams that need to organize email support, assign tickets, publish self-service content and add automation as the queue grows. It is less straightforward if your requirement is a single workspace for email, chat, social, messaging and voice. Freshdesk Omni is a separate product, so confirm which product and plan you are pricing before comparing vendors.</p>
<div class="answer"><strong>Short answer:</strong> Freshdesk is a practical candidate for email-first ticketing and customer self-service. Compare Freshdesk Omni or another platform if your core workflow depends on several live channels in one place.</div>
<h2 id="product">What Freshdesk includes</h2><p>The official Freshdesk pricing page lists ticketing, a shared inbox, customer portal, knowledge base, analytics and reporting across Growth, Pro and Enterprise. The plans add more controls as teams grow. Pro lists custom dashboards, intelligent routing and multiple SLA policies; Enterprise adds features such as skill-based routing, sandbox, audit logs and allowed-domain or IP controls. Check the current feature table for the exact items available in your region.</p><p>Freshworks describes Freshdesk as email-first and Freshdesk Omni as the multichannel product. Omni is intended for teams that manage customer interactions across email, chat, social and other channels in a unified inbox. Do not treat the two products as interchangeable when reading comparisons or estimating cost.</p>
<h2 id="pricing">Pricing checked October 29, 2026</h2><p>The official US pricing page shows the following annual-billing rates for Freshdesk. These are per-agent monthly prices with an annual commitment.</p><div class="publication-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Published annual price</th><th>What stands out</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Growth</th><td>US$19 per agent/month</td><td>Ticketing, shared inbox, customer portal, knowledge base and reporting.</td></tr><tr><th>Pro</th><td>US$55 per agent/month</td><td>Custom dashboards, intelligent routing, multiple SLA policies and other higher-tier controls.</td></tr><tr><th>Enterprise</th><td>US$89 per agent/month</td><td>Skill-based routing, sandbox, audit logs and additional administration controls.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Source: <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Freshdesk official pricing</a>, checked October 29, 2026. The page offers a separate monthly-billing option, and prices may vary by region and tax. Confirm the actual billing cycle and currency in your account before purchase.</p><p>Freshdesk's help article describes a 14-day trial. After the trial, the Freshdesk Free Program can provide two agent seats at no cost for six months. The program applies to Freshdesk, not Freshdesk Omni, and is not a permanent free tier. The same pricing page lists the first 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions included once per account on Growth, Pro and Enterprise. Additional sessions are US$49 per 100, while Freddy AI Copilot is listed at US$29 per agent/month on Pro and Enterprise. Connector tasks and MCP actions have separate metered prices as well.</p><p>These extras matter because a low starting price does not predict the full bill for an AI-heavy workflow. Estimate your ticket volume, expected AI sessions, agent seats, integration tasks and the channels you need before comparing a monthly total with another help desk.</p>
<h2 id="strengths">Potential strengths</h2><ul><li><strong>Familiar ticket workflow:</strong> requests can be assigned, tracked and prioritized rather than left in individual mailboxes.</li><li><strong>Shared inbox and collaboration:</strong> agents can coordinate around a ticket without losing the customer conversation.</li><li><strong>Self-service:</strong> the customer portal and knowledge base help teams publish answers to repeat questions.</li><li><strong>Published plan ladder:</strong> Growth, Pro and Enterprise have visible US annual prices, making an initial seat estimate possible.</li><li><strong>Room to add controls:</strong> higher tiers include more routing, reporting and administration features as the operation grows.</li></ul><p>These points come from Freshworks' official product and pricing materials. They do not mean that every team will get the same outcome. The quality of ticket categories, knowledge content, routing rules and agent adoption still matters.</p>
<h2 id="tradeoffs">Trade-offs and limits to check</h2><h3>Freshdesk versus Freshdesk Omni</h3><p>The first risk is choosing the wrong product. Freshdesk is positioned around email-first help desk work; Omni covers a wider multichannel scope. If your team needs chat, social or messaging in a unified workspace, confirm the correct product, channel support and price before signing up.</p><h3>AI usage is not one flat price</h3><p>The pricing page lists a one-time allowance of 500 AI Agent sessions per account on the paid tiers shown, then charges for additional sessions. Copilot is a separate per-agent add-on on Pro and Enterprise. Forecast your expected volume and confirm how the vendor defines a session. The official pricing FAQ describes an email AI Agent session as a 72-hour window beginning with the customer's first email.</p><h3>Higher-tier reporting and routing</h3><p>Growth may be enough for a team with simple queues. If you need custom dashboards, intelligent routing, multiple SLAs or skill-based routing, check the Pro and Enterprise plan details. Do not assume a feature is included because it appears somewhere on the Freshworks website.</p><h3>Export and migration work</h3><p>Freshdesk provides ticket and account export options, but the export types differ. The official ticket export guide says a filtered ticket export does not include the entire ticket conversation or archived ticket history; an account export is needed for broader account data. Plan for contacts, companies, attachments, comments, knowledge articles, custom fields and reports, not only ticket rows.</p>
<h2 id="fit">Who should use Freshdesk?</h2><p>Freshdesk is a reasonable shortlist choice when the support team works mainly through email, needs a shared ticket queue, wants a customer portal and expects to grow into more automation and reporting. It is also worth considering when a two-agent, six-month Free Program is enough for a short evaluation after the trial.</p><p>Compare alternatives if you need a lightweight shared inbox, deeper CRM-connected service, ecommerce order actions or messaging-led product support. Start with the <a href="/freshdesk/alternatives/">Freshdesk alternatives guide</a>, compare the <a href="/compare/zendesk-vs-freshdesk/">Zendesk vs Freshdesk plans</a>, and read the <a href="/freshdesk/pricing/">Freshdesk pricing guide</a> before deciding.</p>
<h2 id="setup">Setup and migration checklist</h2><ol><li>Confirm whether you need Freshdesk or Freshdesk Omni and list the channels your team will support.</li><li>Choose the first ticket categories, priorities, assignment rules and escalation owners.</li><li>Connect the support email and test the ticket creation, reply and notification flow.</li><li>Build a small set of saved responses and publish knowledge articles for common issues.</li><li>Check the plan's automation, reporting, SLA and AI usage limits before inviting the whole team.</li><li>Export a sample of tickets and verify the fields and date range before moving historical records.</li><li>Test the destination with representative tickets, comments, attachments and contacts before cancelling the old service.</li></ol><p>Freshdesk documents a filtered <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/225158">ticket export workflow</a>, a broader <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/237405-how-can-i-export-tickets-including-the-content-of-the-ticket-">account export for ticket content and historical data</a>, and the <a href="https://developers.freshdesk.com/api/">Freshdesk API</a>. Check the export route that matches the data you need. If you are comparing Zendesk, also read its <a href="/zendesk/how-to-use/">setup guide</a> and the <a href="/zendesk/alternatives/">Zendesk alternatives guide</a>.</p>
<h2 id="method">Review methodology</h2><p>This review uses Freshworks' product page, US pricing page, subscription help article, ticket export instructions and API documentation checked October 29, 2026. It is a research-based assessment, not a hands-on test, customer interview or independent performance benchmark. Plan names, features and prices can change, so use the linked official pages for final verification.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much does Freshdesk cost?</h3><p>The official US pricing page checked October 29, 2026 lists Freshdesk Growth at US$19, Pro at US$55 and Enterprise at US$89 per agent per month when billed annually.</p><h3>Does Freshdesk have a free plan?</h3><p>Freshdesk offers a Free Program for up to two agent seats for six months after the trial, according to its official help article. It is for Freshdesk, not Freshdesk Omni, and is not a permanent free plan.</p><h3>Is Freshdesk the same as Freshdesk Omni?</h3><p>No. Freshdesk is positioned as an email-first help desk. Freshdesk Omni is the separate multichannel product for interactions such as email, chat and social channels.</p><h3>Are Freshdesk AI features included?</h3><p>The pricing page lists 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions included once per account on Growth, Pro and Enterprise. Additional sessions and Freddy AI Copilot have separate charges.</p>
